# The asset vocabulary is digested byte for byte, and coilbox compares its digest
# against the one the hub serves (issue #1708). A checkout that turned these
# bytes into CRLF would hash differently and report every build out of date, so
# the line endings are part of the file's meaning rather than a local preference.
shared/asset-vocabulary.json text eol=lf

# The map catalog is digested and vendored the same way, and for the same reason
# (issue #1735).
shared/map-catalog.json text eol=lf

# These are captures of what pr-downloader printed, and it redraws its progress
# bar with a bare carriage return (issue #1798). One of them arrived with CRLF
# endings, which `core.autocrlf` would quietly flatten on the way in, so the
# tests would be reading something pr-downloader never wrote.
crates/tauri-plugin-coilbox-downloads/tests/fixtures/*.txt -text

# Zero-K's protocol definitions, copied from upstream at a pinned commit.
# `scripts/zerok-refresh.sh` proves that what is vendored is what upstream has by
# comparing the two byte for byte, and two of these files are written with CRLF.
# Normalising them on the way in would leave that check reporting a difference
# nobody can resolve.
crates/coilbox-zerok-protocol/upstream/**/*.cs -text
